[6] where the pressure switches off in an MW-like halo
  condition (gradient, not density): the pressure force competes when
    2 pi G L*^2 |grad rho| ~ g.  For rho ~ r^-n and M ~ 4 pi rho r^3/(3-n):
      R_press = n(3-n)/2 * (L*/r)^2   ->  R = (L*/r)^2 for n = 1 and n = 2.
  So r_switch = L* sqrt(n(3-n)/2) ~ L* : the switch is at ~L*, density-free.
  MW-like NFW (M200 = 1e12 Msun, c = 10): r200 = 211.6 kpc, r_s = 21.16 kpc
  R_press = 1 at r = 24.0181 pc  (L* = 24 pc)  ->  r_switch/L* - 1 = 7.55e-04
K18  PASS r_switch = 24.018 pc   [threshold 24 pc to 1%]  exactly L*: the switch is a length, not a density
  density at the switch: 4.96 Msun/pc^3
  RAR region: the innermost SPARC point is r = 0.080 kpc = 3.3 L*
  R_press at that radius <= (L*/r)^2 = 0.0900 ; at 1 kpc 5.76e-04
K19  PASS r_min = 0.080 kpc (3.3 L*), R = 0.0900   [threshold > 3 L* and R < 0.10]  no conflict with the RAR fit region

